      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T02:08:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Today no domain can call this ioctl. domain.te allowlists only a few F2FS ioctls with allowxperm, so every 0xf5xx ioctl on files goes through xperm filtering, and F2FS_IOC_LOAD_DMABUF (0xf580) is not allowed for any domain.\n\nThe plan is that only a privileged system component (system_server) calls it on behalf of clients through a framework API, as Jaegeuk mentioned. Apps and vendor components will not call it directly. When that lands, the policy will allow F2FS_IOC_LOAD_DMABUF only for that domain and add a neverallowxperm for everyone else. The supported contract is then the framework API, so if we drop the ioctl later, its implementation can fall back to mmap() + preadv2(RWF_DONTCACHE).",
